 the plague he was trying  to find a way to end the poverty problem  in dunwall so he did this by attempting  to kill the poor  using infected rats from a neighboring  continent if a person is infected by the  rat plague symptoms can be as small as  discolored skin or  thinning of hair to its most extreme  which is loss of cognitive functions and  bleeding through the eyes because of the  lack of treatment at this stage in the  outbreak  most people who are infected are  sectioned off from the rest of the  population or just outright killed the  only treatment available is the elixirs  from piero and sokoloff which can help  reduce the symptoms of the plague  the issue is that they are in short  supply and expensive so only the guards  and the rich can afford them you know  the ones  not affected by the plague the reason  why preventative methods became more  extreme in game after we escaped the  prison is that the empress didn't want  to go through such methods but  chinchi's dead in the royal spymasters  in charge he authorized these additional  measures like the watchtowers walls of  light and arc pylons  all of which kill anyone who's not a  guard on sight which we can see a later  mission of a watchtower gunning  civilians down on the nearby bridge  there is also a mandatory dusk to dawn  curfew and anyone who doesn't comply  could also be killed  in most areas there are even large walls  that quarantine sections of the city off  from others preventing people from  either going back to their homes or  trying to leave their homes all in an  effort to stop the spread  it's clear that instead of trying to  cure the population they are waiting for  the plague to kill the poor  while the rest resume their daily  activities all this has been attributed  to dunwall's government and upper class  being more oppressive and obtrusive to  the rest of the population  throughout the area of the game the  player will end up finding signs symbols  and  corpses everywhere there are signs  asking the already suffering residents  to make sacrifices to help better the  rest of the population  there's for sale signs on people's  apartments in hopes they can get money  to afford the elixir of course at the  cost of selling their only home and just  piles of corpses as we could see guards  being instructed to throw dead residents  off a bridge  this is just a simple introduction to  the game's duality but i can't think of  a better showcase of class division  within dishonored 1 than the boyle  mansion and the flood district  in mission 5 we as corvo need to get rid  of lady boyle who is the mistress and  financier to the royal spymaster meaning  she's funding the technologies that are  killing off the population  and separating the rich from the poor  conveniently she's throwing her annual  masquerade party at the mansion so we  can blend in with the guests using our  newly acquired mask  we arrive near a small dock and are  given the whole level to explore  near the mansion is a closed off gate so  that only the party members can attend  it's unclear how the guests who made it  to the party as were the last ones to  arrive but they most likely came by a  railcar as many are seen throughout the  mansion something only the rich have  access to guarding these gates are still  walkers called tall boys purposely made  to keep the guard piloting it out of  reach of weepers and infected rats  they patrol the gates in nearby streets  and will just like everything else in  the guard's arsenal  kill all infected or trespassers on site  on a loudspeaker before we enter we can  hear that by request of the local  landowners that being the boils the  streets are off limits and that any  unauthorized intruders will be dealt  with  this shows that simply by asking the  rich can get what they want  as stated before our mission is to sneak  into the mansion but if we detour away  from the main objective we can go across  the street into the rundown sections of  the district  all the buildings on the outside are  policed by nearby guards equipped with  various floodlights and weaponry to  block off intruders  inside isn't much better as it's covered  with abandoned rooms bloodstains and  graffiti all over the walls  messages written in paint or scratched  on doorways are a common sight  throughout these areas such as death  threats insults and overall just creepy  notes  as for the residents they are either  dead or infected with quite a few  walking the halls of the building  this is already bad enough but just  across the street are the boyle's  mansion  filled with bright lights fireworks and  beautiful architecture it's a complete  slap to the face to any of the residents  residents who aren't rich enough to  afford food to eat and elixir to help  cure the affliction  whereas the boils have more than enough  food for everyone and don't need to  worry about the plague  the outside of the mansion is lined with  streamers rich guests a plethora of  lamps  lavish gardens of flowers and music to  accompany the guests  they of course have the protection of  the local guards so they don't need to  worry about any unwanted guests or rats  sneaking in  and since the party is inside this time  around that means more recreational  activities are dealt with  outside like fencing or dueling all the  guests are dressed in expensive suits  and large over-the-top  masks which fit the theme of the  masquerade party according to some notes  we find out that the sisters also hire  seamstresses and tailors for each guest  that is invited so they have the perfect  outfit for the party  inside is even better looking as soon as  we enter we're greeted with a large  ballroom with shiny white walls  outlining the building  confetti raining from the ceiling and  ornate furnishings connecting each room  is more of the aforementioned design  structures and party favors there's also  a library full of books that could take  years to finish in a s