odies we create the  more blood flies  as deadly as they are when the insect  becomes an adult they lose their wings  and are considered beetles which the  residents of karnaka use for their crops  sometimes bugs do get in people's houses  which is not uncommon but the vast  amount of nests we see in the game is  totally unnatural when the infestation  was at its worst the duke of sirconos  luca abell provided a very detailed  guide on what to do to prevent more  blood flies like cooperation with the  guards instructions on cremation  and other preventative measures but  eventually he stopped funding the  project which caused the bloodfly  infestation to skyrocket and now the  only people able to exterminate them  are brave civilians possibly wanting to  do some quick coin  as the amber inside the nests are quite  valuable but considering they don't have  the weaponry the local guard carries  most of these people end up dying  which once again leads more blood flies  creating a never-ending cycle there's  also a disease that these blood flies  carry too  not every nest these flies make are dead  bodies some  are considered alive the blood flies lay  their eggs in the body of a person  this also causes their cognitive  functions to cease where the only thing  on their mind is ensuring the safety of  the nest  if they're killed a swarm of flies will  erupt from them making it even more of a  hassle to deal with i wanted to explain  the danger these insects pose to the  citizens of karnaka now as i'll be using  them to make a point in the future  arcane studios also did a really good  job of hiding these issues from the  player before we set foot there  after the first hour or so of missions  we and megan foster set out to karnaka  for the first time  and it was breathtaking the city is  coined as the jewel at the edge of the  world and it's truly a beautiful city  railways going across the ocean large  towers and trees  windmills on every corner and not to  mention the giant mountain in the  background which is such a magnificent  sight but it's all because we're on the  outside looking in from the moment we  step on the dock it loses that beauty as  we turn left we see blood in the water  coming from the sewer system they stock  in most likely a large part  of the port is dedicated to whale  hunting most of the good equipment seems  to be out of reach of the regular  population so some have taken to selling  it under the table so to speak is this a  variety of black market shops that can  sell us elixir upgrades and other  equipment and nearby we can also see our  first introduction to the blood fly  infestation  outside is three people arguing about  the plan they seem to be very indecisive  about going in  as they're unsure if there's even any  money inside the house and if the risk  is worth the reward we can also see that  once the flies move in the house is  totally inhabitable not only are the  flies an issue because of the risk of  being stung and becoming a host there's  also a wax-like material that is molded  together to hold up these nests which  makes it even harder for the nest to be  cleaned out i wouldn't be surprised if  many people could never return back to  their homes even if the nests were gone  as the additional material covers up  more surface area than the actual hive  itself  this then leads us to dr hypatia she's  one of our targets in game but she's  also working on curing the blood fly  fever that numerous residents have  experienced which is great  except the duke is to blame for keeping  her trapped at the institute in fact i'd  go as far to say the duke is the cause  for everything happening in karnaka  the previous duke was thedonia sabelle  he was very well respected amongst  everyone in karnaka the gangs like the  abbey and the howlers as well as the  regular citizens both rich and poor  when the donis died he passed the power  to his son luke abell the current duke  his ruling of circonus but 