 library a vault that hides delilah's  soul but also doubles as another library  and floors upon floors of different  rooms for the guests and other  activities and best of all  no blood flies the reason i bring this  up about the duke is i'd like to argue  that the duke is just as bad if not  worse than the royal spymaster to an  extent the rat plague affected both the  rich and poor  we can see in the boyle mansion the  occasional rats sneak inside it's  obvious that the poor were affected more  than the rich aristocrats but it  affected them albeit very small we could  see some aristocrats argued during the  party about their businesses  one saying that he won't make as much  due to most of his land being covered in  corpses and rats  so it's clear that some rich are  affected by the plague but the blood  flies the dust mines and the poverty  problem  only affect the poor in karnaka most of  karnaka's districts are overrun with  local gangs and people in poverty  living in run-down buildings with  chipped walls broken stairs and graffiti  on every wall  some aren't even able to live in  buildings thanks to the blood flies the  miners themselves are overworked and  exhausted some  dying from exhaustion while those who  survive are being poisoned from the  terrible air quality inside the mines  in the other districts is where most of  the blood fly infestations are and while  there was a plan to eradicate them the  duke stopped funding the program which  caused more people to die  more houses to be lost and more blood  flies to be born causing a never-ending  cycle the only person who was willing to  help was dr hypatia who was working to  solve both issues but she was placed at  the institute  and trapped her under the duke's rule  only letting her out when he wanted to  this was all happening while the duke  was according to megan  living a relaxing life sipping wine and  having daily orgies and anyone who  attempted to stop him was immediately  put down by the guards  so i leave the question to you who given  the circumstances of each city and  nation  is the worst the royal spymaster the  creator of the plague on an attempt to  solve the poverty problem of dunwall  only to have it spread too quickly  causing mass genocide and sending those  who are infected to their deaths or the  duke a tyrannical ruler who kills anyone  who disagrees with him refusing to fix  the infestation and instead overworks  the miners till they collapse so he can  fund his rich palace  this is what i mean by the duality of  dishonored both games showcase the  insane amount of power the rich have  over the poor and it only gets bigger as  the days go on  letting the rich continue to enjoy their  life in the city while the poor fend for  themselves without any assistance from  the government  that government being the one who caused  the problems in the first place  all right i think i've talked enough for  one video so we're going to be moving on  to the outro portion of the video which  means that can be a little bit more  informal with my wording thank you all  for watching today's video  let me know what you think about it in  the comments down below also like i  brought up before with the recent deal  between bethesda and xbox dishonored is  now on game pass so this is perfect  timing for those who are new to the  series it's one of my all-time favorites  like always subscribe if you're new for  more narrative commentaries like this  one on all your favorite games and if  you're a returning viewer i thank you  for coming back  if you want to watch another video of  mine i highly recommend my previous  upload which  talked about far cry and why the  villains are so well written within the  series  with that take care everyone hopefully  i'll see you in another video in the  future  and goodbye  [Music]  you

