  the district  all the buildings on the outside are  policed by nearby guards equipped with  various floodlights and weaponry to  block off intruders  inside isn't much better as it's covered  with abandoned rooms bloodstains and  graffiti all over the walls  messages written in paint or scratched  on doorways are a common sight  throughout these areas such as death  threats insults and overall just creepy  notes  as for the residents they are either  dead or infected with quite a few  walking the halls of the building  this is already bad enough but just  across the street are the boyle's  mansion  filled with bright lights fireworks and  beautiful architecture it's a complete  slap to the face to any of the residents  residents who aren't rich enough to  afford food to eat and elixir to help  cure the affliction  whereas the boils have more than enough  food for everyone and don't need to  worry about the plague  the outside of the mansion is lined with  streamers rich guests a plethora of  lamps  lavish gardens of flowers and music to  accompany the guests  they of course have the protection of  the local guards so they don't need to  worry about any unwanted guests or rats  sneaking in  and since the party is inside this time  around that means more recreational  activities are dealt with  outside like fencing or dueling all the  guests are dressed in expensive suits  and large over-the-top  masks which fit the theme of the  masquerade party according to some notes  we find out that the sisters also hire  seamstresses and tailors for each guest  that is invited so they have the perfect  outfit for the party  inside is even better looking as soon as  we enter we're greeted with a large  ballroom with shiny white walls  outlining the building  confetti raining from the ceiling and  ornate furnishings connecting each room  is more of the aforementioned design  structures and party favors there's also  a library full of books that could take  years to finish in a small room that  doubles as a relaxing place for guests  to sit and eat as well as showing off  the numerous trophies that they have did  i also forget to mention that this was  only the first floor as upstairs is  where the boyle sisters sleep i should  probably explain by now that the boils  are triplets which is the main point of  the mission we have to find out which  one is our correct target  but this shows that it's not just one  sister's wealth being poured into the  party it's all three of theirs  all the sisters have their own rooms and  wings that include things like paintings  aging pieces of art separate bathrooms  and much more  they clearly live a lavish lifestyle and  don't mind letting others know  considering the vast amount of wealth  they use just to host the party  the boyle's mansion is the epitome of  showing off flaunting their wealth to  the poor who are so desperately trying  to survive while the rich and wealthy  ignore the issues outside the walls and  enjoy a relaxing evening  the other side of the colon would be the  flooded district of dunwall  playable during mission 7 the flooded  district was flooded due to the nearby  dam breaking and causing all the water  from the river to steamroll the  district's infrastructure most of it is  occupied by the whalers a gang led by  the assassin dowd but some of the areas  are in control by the local guard this  whole district is an issue in itself not  only are the people's homes destroyed  leaving them to just wander the streets  or  what's left of them there's dowd's gangs  betraying the rooftops and the whole  place was sectioned off by the rest of  dunwall this is because instead of  fixing the district the government under  the royal spymaster's rule turned it  into a mass grave when we finally escape  the majority of the flooded areas we  walk past some rubble to see a rail car  dumping dozens of bodies out of it right  on top of where we're walking  this place is practically a trashy  internment camp all the city's garbage  from traditional trash  whale bones and corpses go in here  there's also quite a lot of infected  people here too  as anyone who agrees to the royal  spymaster's rehabilitation program  whether they've volunteered or not  is send here to be quarantined away from  everyone the disease is going to kill  them anyway so why waste the whale oil  to drive their corpses over to the  district when you could just put them in  the district to begin with  it's like digging your own grave except  this time it's already dug the moment  you're dragged in here of course the  district is surrounded by large arc  pylons walls of light and other  machinery to prevent people from  escaping  they are forcing the people to stay in  the district and give them no option to  leave  like i said you're dead the moment you  walk in and that rail car comes quite  frequently you could say this is done on  purpose as this is a way to escape the  district so it's more of a gameplay  mechanic but if we were to shut that out  of our minds for a moment  it's insane how fast this comes back  with the number of bodies it has  every couple of minutes or so it comes  by and pours dozens of corpses into the  district letting them rot and it keeps  coming back with more and more bodies  i did do a bit of research for this on  the wikipedias i couldn't find any info  in game but apparently dunwall had a  population of around 2 million before  the plague and  currently in-game is around 200 000  people left so just think about that for  a moment there are tons of areas like  this  in fact all areas are very much the same  with having run down buildings  patrolling guards and dead bodies along  the streets  but i want to dial it back to the chaos  discussion as i said earlier the chaos  level determines the ending of the game  and while it also changes the ending  mission  the after credit narration is what i  want to focus on more should the player  kill little to no one in their  playthrough they'll get the low chaos  ending which he's emily become empress  with the rest of the residents clearly  having happier spirits  because we decided to not act out and  kill others piero and sulkeloff can be  seen combining their separate formulas  into a new elixir that can cure the  plague which as the outsider states  brings up a golden age of dunwall where  the plague eventually becomes eradicated  alternatively if we kill lots of people  throughout our playthrough we received  the high chaos ending which shows emily  becoming the empress except no one is  happy and can be seen arguing at one  another as one even attempts to harm  lady emily there are also scenes of  corruption and gang violence as some  members can be seen looting  corpses the red plague isn't even close  to being dealt with if anything it's  grown thanks to the vast amount of  corpses we left behind harboring the  disease  this is clearly not a great ending and  thankfully the canon option for  dishonored 2  is the low chaos one and speaking of  that let's transition to dishonored  sequel as the duality between the rich  and poor and karnaka is arguably just as  bad if not worse even with the lack of a  citywide plague  dishonored 2 as stated before is 15  years in the future the rat plague is  gone and things are going smoothly with  emily being the current empress that is  until her supposed aunt delilah claims  she is the rightful heir and throws us  out the game then gives us the option to  play as corvo again or  emily personally i've always thought  emily was the canon choice so i chose  her for both playthroughs and that's how  i'll be referencing certain parts in the  video with her as the main character  the chaos system also makes a return in  dishonored 2 but there's no plague so  what changes well karnaka has a bit of a  blood fly infestation these are native  insects to karnaka and they will make  their nests in abandoned homes and dead  bodies so the more bodies we create the  more blood flies  as deadly as they are when the insect  becomes an adult they lose their wings  and are considered beetles which the  residents of karnaka use for their crops  sometimes bugs do get in people's houses  which is not uncommon but the vast  amount of nests we see in the game is  totally unnatural when the infestation  was at its worst the duke of sirconos  luca abell provided a very detailed  guide on what to do to prevent more  blood flies like cooperation with the  guards instructions on cremation  and other preventative measures but  eventually he stopped funding the  project which caused the bloodfly  infestation to skyrocket and now the  only people able to exterminate them  are brave civilians possibly wanting to  do some quick coin  as the amber inside the nests are quite  valuable but considering they don't have  the weaponry the local guard carries  most of these people end up dying  which once again leads more blood flies  creating a never-ending cycle there's  also a disease that these blood flies  carry too  not every nest these flies make are dead  bodies some  are considered alive the blood flies lay  their eggs in the body of a person  this also causes their cognitive  functions to cease where the only thing  on their mind is ensuring the safety of  the nest  if they're killed a swarm of flies will  erupt from them making it even more of a  hassle to deal with i wanted to explain  the danger these insects pose to the  citizens of karnaka now as i'll be using  them to make a point in the future  arcane studios also did a really good  job of hiding these issues from the  player before we set foot there  after the first hour or so of missions  we and megan foster set out to karnaka  for the first time  and it was breathtaking the city is  coined as the jewel at the edge of the  world and it's truly a beautiful city  railways going across the ocean large  towers and trees  windmills on every corner and not to  mention the giant mountain in the  background which is such a magnificent  sight but it's all because we're on the  outside looking in from the moment we  step on the dock it loses that beauty as  we turn left we see blood in the water  coming from the sewer system they stock  in most likely a large part  of the port is dedicated to whale  hunting most of the good equipment seems  to be out of reach of the regular  population so some have taken to selling  it under the table so to speak is this a  variety of black market shops that can  sell us elixir upgrades and other  equipment and nearby we can also see our  first introduction to the blood fly  infestation  outside is three people arguing about  the plan they seem to be very indecisive  about going in  as they're unsure if there's even any  money inside the house and if the risk  is worth the reward we can also see that  once the flies move in the house is  totally inhabitable not only are the  flies an issue because of the risk of  being stung and becoming a host there's  also a wax-like material that is molded  together to hold up these nests which  makes it even harder for the nest to be  cleaned out i wouldn't be surprised if  many people could never return back to  their homes even if the nests were gone  as the additional material covers up  more surface area than the actual hive  itself  this then leads us to dr hypatia she's  one of our targets in game but she's  also working on curing the blood fly  fever that numerous residents have  experienced which is great  except the duke is to blame for keeping  her trapped at the institute in fact i'd  go as far to say the duke is the cause  for everything happening in karnaka  the previous duke was thedonia sabelle  he was very well respected amongst  everyone in karnaka the gangs like the  abbey and the howlers as well as the  regular citizens both rich and poor  when the donis died he passed the power  to his son luke abell the current duke  his ruling of circonus but more  specifically karnaka is quite the  opposite of his father  luke despises the abbey and he uses his  power to oppress the people of sirconos  using his authority to shut down any  rebellions that may spark up kinda  sounds like someone else we just talked  about luke's father was also friends  with aramis stilton who is the owner of  the mines here in karnaka but thanks to  his eventual insanity he would give up  control of the minds of the duke who  while doubling the profits of the mines  more than likely made the conditions  worse for the workers in the process  this is also the cause for the constant  dust storms we see in the dust district  his reasoning for overworking the miners  was so that he could afford his lavish  lifestyle this not only caused more  people to be sick because of the  conditions of the mines but also be  exhausted and collapse while working to  make matters worse the howlers a local  gang  wanted more territory and attempted to  set up in the dust district this is at  the same time the abbey wanted the  territory for their own to build a  chapel with the guards being overrun by  two gangs they pulled out of the  district and put up security checkpoints  with  walls of light surrounding the district  so nobody could escape that means that  anyone that just happened to live in the  district with no affiliation of the  gangs now has to suffer the consequences  going back to that statement about his  lavish lifestyle we had an up close look  at his mansion in mission 8 where we  attempt to assassinate the duke  according to emily the grand palace  costs enough money to feed the people of  karnaka for years so instead of  supplying more food for those in need he  decided to make a lavish mansion instead  and within seconds you can already tell  just by looking that the palace is made  of way different material than the  houses in the other districts  more rooms than you can count including  separate rooms for his bed and work  quarters  a library a vault that hides delilah's  soul but also doubles as another library  and floors upon floors of different  rooms for the guests and other  activities and best of all  no blood flies the reason i bring this  up about the duke is i'd like to argue  that the duke is just as bad if not  worse than the royal spymaster to an  extent the rat plague affected both the  rich and poor  we can see in the boyle mansion the  occasional rats sneak inside it's  obvious that the poor were affected more  than the rich aristocrats but it  affected them albeit very small we could  see some aristocrats argued during the  party about their businesses  one saying that he won't make as much  due to most of his land being covered in  corpses and rats  so it's clear that some rich are  affected by the plague but the blood  flies the dust mines and the poverty  problem  only affect the poor in karnaka most of  karnaka's districts are overrun with  local gangs and people in poverty  living in run-down buildings with  chipped walls broken stairs and graffiti  on every wall  some aren't even able to live in  buildings thanks to the blood flies the  miners themselves are overworked and  exhausted some  dying from exhaustion while those who  survive are being poisoned from the  terrible air quality inside the mines  in the other districts is where most of  the blood fly infestations are and while  there was a plan to eradicate them the  duke stopped funding the program which  caused more people to die  more houses to be lost and more blood  flies to be born causing a never-ending  cycle the only person who was willing to  help was dr hypatia who was working to  solve both issues but she was placed at  the institute  and trapped her under the duke's rule  only letting her out when he wanted to  this was all happening while the duke  was according to megan  living a relaxing life sipping wine and  having daily orgies and anyone who  attempted to stop him was immediately  put down by the guards  so i leave the question to you who given  the circumstances of each city and  nation  is the worst the royal spymaster the  creator of the plague on an attempt to  solve the poverty problem of dunwall  only to have it spread too quickly  causing mass genocide and sending those  who are infected to their deaths or the  duke a tyrannical ruler who kills anyone  who disagrees with him refusing to fix  the infestation and instead overworks  the miners till they collapse so he can  fund his rich palace  this is what i mean by the duality of  dishonored both games showcase the  insane amount of power the rich have  over the poor and it only gets bigger as  the days go on  letting the rich continue to enjoy their  life in the city while the poor fend for  themselves without any assistance from  the government  that government being the one who caused  the problems in the first place  all right i think i've talked enough for  one video so we're going to be moving on  to the outro portion of the video which  means that can be a little bit more  informal with my wording thank you all  for watching today's video  let me know what you think about it in  the comments down below also like i  brought up before with the recent deal  between bethesda and xbox dishonored is  now on game pass so this is perfect  timing for those who are new to the  series it's one of my all-time favorites  like always subscribe if you're new for  more narrative commentaries like this  one on all your favorite games and if  you're a returning viewer i thank you  for coming back  if you want to watch another video of  mine i highly recommend my previous  upload which  talked about far cry and why the  villains are so well written within the  series  with that take care everyone hopefully  i'll see you in another video in the  future  and goodbye  [Music]  you
 

